WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.140
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.410 --> 01:34.910
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.229 --> 01:37.720
[Episode 42]

4
01:38.590 --> 01:39.150
Guo.

5
01:39.229 --> 01:40.280
We add the soy sauce and vinegar

6
01:40.310 --> 01:41.590
right out in the open.

7
01:41.590 --> 01:43.120
Why do you call it "sneaking in"?

8
01:43.150 --> 01:43.870
Yeah, exactly.

9
01:43.870 --> 01:45.120
See, you guys just don't get it.

10
01:45.680 --> 01:47.710
"Sneaking in" the vinegar means

11
01:47.840 --> 01:49.680
you can't go overboard.

12
01:49.789 --> 01:52.479
You want to bring out its rich and savory flavor,

13
01:52.670 --> 01:54.420
but without actually making it sour!

14
01:54.789 --> 01:56.380
There's a real knack to it.

15
01:56.680 --> 01:58.200
Heat the wok and oil.

16
01:58.479 --> 02:00.320
First, stir-fry the pork belly

17
02:00.350 --> 02:01.680
and sauté them up a bit.

18
02:02.120 --> 02:04.120
The drier the meat, the better.

19
02:04.900 --> 02:07.700
And the more oil, the better.

20
02:08.110 --> 02:09.539
The more oil, the more fragrant.

21
02:10.000 --> 02:11.910
Stir-fry over high heat.

22
02:12.620 --> 02:14.470
Stir-fry the meat

23
02:14.490 --> 02:17.820
until it sizzles with oil

24
02:18.030 --> 02:20.030
and the whole room smells great.

25
02:22.160 --> 02:23.390
Guo, Guo.

26
02:23.510 --> 02:24.550
Are you okay, Guo?

27
02:24.700 --> 02:26.230
Guo, are you okay?

28
02:26.560 --> 02:27.430
I'm fine.

29
02:27.880 --> 02:28.880
Then take a rest.

30
02:29.040 --> 02:30.650
I'll cook for everyone, okay?

31
02:30.680 --> 02:31.840
Okay.

32
02:34.990 --> 02:38.120
I'll cook a famous Jiangxi dish for everyone,

33
02:38.560 --> 02:39.560
Yugan-Style Stir-Fried Pork with Chili.

34
02:39.579 --> 02:40.140
Okay.

35
02:40.170 --> 02:41.340
Great, I love this.

36
02:41.960 --> 02:42.910
To cook this dish,

37
02:43.320 --> 02:45.110
you need Fengshu chili from Yugan County

38
02:45.190 --> 02:46.030
and pork belly.

39
02:46.340 --> 02:48.710
The pork belly must be 70% fat and 30% lean.

40
02:49.150 --> 02:50.280
The more fat, the better.

41
02:50.840 --> 02:52.910
The fatter it is, the more fragrant the oil will be.

42
02:52.910 --> 02:53.470
Yes.

43
02:55.000 --> 02:55.630
And also,

44
02:55.870 --> 02:56.560
when cooking this dish,

45
02:56.960 --> 02:58.360
the most important thing is the heat.

46
02:59.520 --> 03:00.400
At the beginning,

47
03:00.870 --> 03:03.030
dry-fry the chili first.

48
03:03.240 --> 03:04.520
When it's fragrant,

49
03:04.800 --> 03:05.870
take it out and set it aside.

50
03:06.520 --> 03:07.960
Add a little more oil

51
03:08.000 --> 03:09.600
and put the pork belly in.

52
03:09.650 --> 03:11.370
Let it sizzle

53
03:11.760 --> 03:13.080
and stir-fry slowly over low heat.

54
03:13.290 --> 03:14.560
When the oil comes out,

55
03:14.720 --> 03:16.680
add minced ginger and fermented black beans.

56
03:16.700 --> 03:18.050
After it's fragrant,

57
03:18.320 --> 03:20.720
put the chili back in.

58
03:20.910 --> 03:21.560
Remember,

59
03:21.710 --> 03:23.400
the heat must be high at this time.

60
03:23.590 --> 03:24.750
Stir-fry it a few more times.

61
03:24.770 --> 03:26.220
Then "sneak in" some vinegar.

62
03:26.360 --> 03:27.280
It'll be so savory.

63
03:27.310 --> 03:28.190
"Sneaking in" vinegar again?

64
03:28.400 --> 03:29.400
You learned it so fast.

65
03:29.600 --> 03:30.560
Nonsense.

66
03:30.579 --> 03:32.500
Why "sneak in" vinegar now?

67
03:33.090 --> 03:35.090
Guo, don't interrupt.

68
03:35.470 --> 03:36.800
I'm cooking now.

69
03:36.820 --> 03:38.310
If I say "sneak in" some vinegar, that's exactly what we do.

70
03:38.680 --> 03:40.750
Besides, "sneaking in" some vinegar enhances the flavor.

71
03:40.750 --> 03:42.120
It'll definitely be delicious.

72
03:42.300 --> 03:45.460
If you put too much, it's not "sneaking in".

73
03:45.600 --> 03:46.320
Remember.

74
03:46.340 --> 03:48.310
Don't sprinkle too much salt.

75
03:48.340 --> 03:49.750
If you put too much, it'll be too salty.

76
03:50.150 --> 03:51.280
Because there are fermented black beans.

77
03:51.480 --> 03:52.950
The fermented black beans are also salty.

78
03:53.710 --> 03:55.240
Finally, we add yellow wine.

79
03:55.329 --> 03:56.120
Guo.

80
03:56.180 --> 03:58.230
Gou Yazi said to add yellow wine.

81
03:58.260 --> 03:59.290
Is that right?

82
04:00.280 --> 04:01.000
Guo.

83
04:01.590 --> 04:03.470
Is it right to add yellow wine?

84
04:03.630 --> 04:05.120
Sneaking in vinegar brings out the flavor.

85
04:05.800 --> 04:06.520
Guo.

86
04:07.390 --> 04:09.280
Just wait till you taste it. It's going be delicious!

87
04:09.310 --> 04:10.190
Guo.

88
04:11.290 --> 04:12.050
Guo.

89
04:12.070 --> 04:14.470
-Guo. -Guo.

90
04:14.960 --> 04:17.120
-Guo. -Guo.

91
04:17.390 --> 04:18.870
-Guo. -Guo.

92
04:18.870 --> 04:19.510
Where's the water?

93
04:19.750 --> 04:20.720
Bring some water.

94
04:21.279 --> 04:22.490
Water, water.

95
04:23.390 --> 04:24.870
-Guo. -Guo.

96
04:25.670 --> 04:29.340
Medic! Call the medic over! Medic!

97
04:30.690 --> 04:31.860
-Guo. -Guo.

98
04:31.950 --> 04:32.659
Guo.

99
04:35.480 --> 04:36.190
Wake up, Guo.

100
04:36.230 --> 04:36.790
Wake up.

101
04:37.560 --> 04:38.560
-Guo. -Guo.

102
04:40.360 --> 04:41.240
Guo.

103
04:43.070 --> 04:43.820
How is he?

104
04:44.480 --> 04:45.750
Guo is gone.

105
04:46.390 --> 04:47.000
Guo.

106
04:47.430 --> 04:50.800
-Guo! -Guo!

107
05:50.520 --> 05:52.450
Gou Yazi, get up!

108
05:53.130 --> 05:54.490
Look at these people in the Red Army.

109
05:54.540 --> 05:55.860
Who would dare disobey an order?

110
05:56.310 --> 05:57.310
Look at you.

111
05:57.570 --> 05:59.409
You still want to avenge your father?

112
05:59.550 --> 06:01.300
Go home and avenge him from your bed!

113
06:01.710 --> 06:02.510
Now you know

114
06:02.510 --> 06:04.430
the thing left by your dad is precious.

115
06:04.450 --> 06:06.640
Then isn't my wok precious?

116
06:06.860 --> 06:09.130
My son Gousheng died

117
06:09.450 --> 06:11.520
protecting that wok.

118
06:12.070 --> 06:14.830
Gou Yazi, throw the wok away!

119
06:15.390 --> 06:16.360
The wok can't be thrown away.

120
06:16.380 --> 06:18.900
You kid, you value wealth over your life.

121
06:19.190 --> 06:20.840
You take after me in this.

122
06:22.650 --> 06:24.170
I got you assigned to the mess unit

123
06:24.400 --> 06:26.160
because you look like my son.

124
06:26.520 --> 06:28.450
If you have a pair of big ears sticking out,

125
06:28.680 --> 06:29.800
you'd look even more like him.

126
06:43.570 --> 06:44.890
Guo.

127
07:08.360 --> 07:09.160
Huang.

128
07:11.750 --> 07:12.560
Commander.

129
07:14.350 --> 07:16.720
Are all the headquarters' animals here?

130
07:17.630 --> 07:19.710
Including Dahei, there are only 6 left.

131
07:19.730 --> 07:20.620
They are all here.

132
07:23.680 --> 07:24.360
Kill them.

133
07:24.910 --> 07:25.390
Commander.

134
07:25.410 --> 07:26.240
This is an order.

135
07:26.680 --> 07:29.600
Not a single piece of meat is to be left at the headquarters.

136
07:29.970 --> 07:32.360
Send some to the stretcher team.

137
07:32.680 --> 07:33.950
Distribute the rest to the regiments.

138
07:34.210 --> 07:35.330
Soldiers get the good meat.

139
07:35.890 --> 07:37.930
Cadres get the offal.

140
07:39.470 --> 07:40.150
Execute the order.

141
07:40.180 --> 07:40.740
Yes, sir.

142
07:52.610 --> 07:53.960
Y-You can't take Dahei!

143
07:54.190 --> 07:55.230
You can't take Dahei!

144
07:55.320 --> 07:56.680
This is the Commander's mule.

145
07:56.720 --> 07:57.040
Huang.

146
07:57.060 --> 07:59.420
Whoever lays a hand on Dahei will have to go through me!

147
08:05.200 --> 08:07.610
Commander, Dahei can't be killed.

148
08:08.000 --> 08:09.450
When crossing the Xiang River,

149
08:09.640 --> 08:11.640
I only made it by holding onto its tail.

150
08:11.690 --> 08:14.100
It carried 3 wounded soldiers over the snowy mountains.

151
08:14.260 --> 08:15.990
Dahei has earned its merits.

152
11:30.480 --> 11:31.150
What's wrong?

153
11:31.480 --> 11:32.240
Tell me.

154
11:32.630 --> 11:34.270
Let the comrades rest a bit.

155
11:35.150 --> 11:36.350
I can walk by myself.

156
11:37.440 --> 11:38.890
This is my first time being your leader.

157
11:39.240 --> 11:40.600
Obey orders and follow commands.

158
11:40.600 --> 11:41.270
Okay?

159
11:41.870 --> 11:42.670
If you get down now,

160
11:42.670 --> 11:44.440
aren't you causing trouble for the comrades?

161
11:45.120 --> 11:46.270
But it's very good.

162
11:46.600 --> 11:47.840
Make as many requests as you want.

163
11:48.270 --> 11:50.060
I won't agree to all of them.

164
11:50.440 --> 11:51.160
Chen Geng.

165
11:52.560 --> 11:53.290
Lisan.

166
11:55.260 --> 11:57.620
Lisan, why didn't you say anything?

167
11:58.060 --> 11:59.630
Come here.

168
11:59.930 --> 12:01.130
Someone come over and take over.

169
12:01.200 --> 12:01.750
Okay.

170
12:03.310 --> 12:03.990
Let me do it.

171
12:04.020 --> 12:06.500
[Yang Lisan, Director of the General Logistics Department of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

172
12:05.120 --> 12:06.230
I don't trust anyone else to carry him.

173
12:06.600 --> 12:07.360
Move aside.

174
12:11.040 --> 12:13.310
Nineteen years later, in 1954,

175
12:13.910 --> 12:15.750
the Chinese People's Liberation Army's

176
12:15.750 --> 12:17.960
Minister of Finance, Yang Lisan,

177
12:18.040 --> 12:19.470
passed away from illness.

178
12:20.550 --> 12:22.320
Premier of the State Council Zhou Enlai

179
12:22.370 --> 12:25.260
insisted on personally carrying the bier for Yang Lisan's funeral.

180
12:26.320 --> 12:27.080
He said,

181
12:27.630 --> 12:29.870
"We Communists are atheists,

182
12:30.240 --> 12:32.030
but we are not heartless.

183
12:32.760 --> 12:34.250
Back when we were crossing the grasslands,

184
12:34.780 --> 12:38.460
Yang Lisan carried me back from the brink of death.

185
12:39.200 --> 12:42.360
Today, I should help carry him on his final journey."

186
14:51.850 --> 14:52.680
Zhang Side.

187
14:55.370 --> 14:56.210
Zhang Side.

188
14:56.900 --> 14:59.300
There are gullies everywhere here.

189
14:59.830 --> 15:01.400
Put me down.

190
15:01.520 --> 15:02.310
Squad Leader.

191
15:02.940 --> 15:03.910
I'll carry you.

192
15:03.930 --> 15:06.050
I must carry you out.

193
15:10.160 --> 15:12.280
Put me down.

194
15:14.890 --> 15:17.010
Squad Leader, let's cross the puddle.

195
15:24.550 --> 15:25.470
Squad Leader, how are you?

196
15:25.960 --> 15:26.670
I'm fine.

197
15:26.670 --> 15:27.440
Glad you're fine.

198
15:27.440 --> 15:28.790
Are you okay?

199
15:43.340 --> 15:44.520
Squad Leader, how are you?

200
15:44.550 --> 15:45.030
I'm fine.

201
15:45.330 --> 15:46.880
Hurry up and rest for a while.

202
