336
29:40.920 --> 29:44.510
The grassland on this day in late August 1935

337
29:44.850 --> 29:46.330
was so quiet.

338
29:47.750 --> 29:51.000
There was no sound of wind or water.

339
29:51.250 --> 29:53.810
Even the mist seemed to have frozen.

340
29:55.830 --> 29:56.510
Under the sky,

341
29:56.510 --> 29:59.230
only these 700-plus young soldiers were left.

342
30:00.110 --> 30:02.550
They were only one step away from victory,

343
30:03.220 --> 30:06.420
but due to extreme hunger, illness, and hypothermia,

344
30:06.850 --> 30:09.480
they left their lives forever on the grassland,

345
30:10.410 --> 30:12.610
without even having their names recorded.

346
30:14.640 --> 30:15.920
Many years later,

347
30:16.890 --> 30:19.330
whenever General Wang Ping recalled them,

348
30:19.840 --> 30:21.560
he would still burst into tears.

349
30:22.640 --> 30:23.440
He regretted

350
30:23.710 --> 30:25.110
that he couldn't even figure out

351
30:25.110 --> 30:26.720
the designation of this unit.

352
30:28.350 --> 30:30.750
What they took away was illness and hunger.

353
30:30.950 --> 30:33.320
What they left behind was dawn and victory.

354
30:34.510 --> 30:35.440
Today,

355
30:35.730 --> 30:36.730
this memory

356
30:36.760 --> 30:39.040
is forever engraved on the Banyou Monument to the Fallen Soldiers

357
30:39.330 --> 30:41.140
of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army

358
30:41.140 --> 30:42.960
at the banks of the Banyou River.

359
30:45.970 --> 30:49.100
Is anyone there?

360
30:50.650 --> 30:53.500
Is anyone there?

361
30:54.880 --> 30:56.720
Is anyone there?

362
30:58.030 --> 30:58.720
Yes.

363
31:00.490 --> 31:00.990
Yes.

364
31:01.030 --> 31:03.270
Is anyone there?

365
31:03.270 --> 31:06.030
Is anyone there?

366
31:09.440 --> 31:11.510
Is anyone there?

367
31:15.950 --> 31:17.030
Is anyone there?

368
31:17.050 --> 31:19.470
Is anyone there?

369
31:20.240 --> 31:21.750
Is anyone there?

370
31:21.750 --> 31:24.310
Answer me!

371
31:27.720 --> 31:29.310
Is anyone there?

372
31:30.110 --> 31:32.750
Is anyone there?

373
31:36.310 --> 31:38.110
Is anyone there?

374
31:41.980 --> 31:44.830
Is anyone there?

375
31:45.570 --> 31:48.280
Answer if you hear us!

376
32:23.350 --> 32:24.160
Take shelter from the rain.

377
32:24.350 --> 32:25.720
Everyone, take shelter.

378
32:25.970 --> 32:27.530
Quick. Set up the tents.

379
32:28.240 --> 32:29.520
Come on. Set up the tents.

380
32:33.880 --> 32:35.510
Camp here.

381
32:37.170 --> 32:37.930
Chairman.

382
32:45.960 --> 32:46.720
Get under here.

383
32:46.720 --> 32:47.480
Everyone, take shelter from the rain.

384
32:48.440 --> 32:49.110
Quick!

385
32:49.110 --> 32:50.030
Watch out for the hail.

386
32:51.370 --> 32:53.460
Take shelter. Take shelter.

387
32:55.200 --> 32:56.000
Coming.

388
36:19.750 --> 36:21.500
The bravery and tenacity of the Red Army

389
36:21.730 --> 36:23.290
must not be spent in needless sacrifice,

390
36:23.760 --> 36:26.070
and they must not become an excuse for our blind command!

391
36:26.500 --> 36:28.800
If the main force of the Red Army is lost,

392
36:28.960 --> 36:30.290
what will be left?

393
36:30.840 --> 36:33.590
How is the Chinese revolution to go on?

394
36:35.630 --> 36:36.360
Comrades.

395
36:37.260 --> 36:40.780
Right now, we are standing at this crossroads.

396
36:41.070 --> 36:43.800
Either we head towards destruction,

397
36:44.450 --> 36:47.490
or we head towards a new life.

398
36:51.360 --> 36:53.110
With every artillery shell that falls,

399
36:53.630 --> 36:56.880
a swath of our Red Army soldiers falls.

400
36:57.020 --> 36:58.580
Every piece of shrapnel

401
36:58.930 --> 37:01.340
is tearing at the bodies of our soldiers.

402
37:01.890 --> 37:04.770
The water of the Xiang River has turned red!

403
37:05.230 --> 37:08.630
Now there is only one way: fight to the death to survive!

404
37:10.600 --> 37:11.340
Fish.

405
37:11.770 --> 37:12.810
There are fish.

406
37:13.380 --> 37:14.700
Fish, fish.

407
37:15.030 --> 37:17.110
Fish.

408
37:17.950 --> 37:18.950
There are fish.

409
37:19.060 --> 37:19.790
Fish.

410
37:19.820 --> 37:20.570
Fish.

411
37:25.000 --> 37:25.760
There are fish.

412
37:41.110 --> 37:42.060
Fish.

413
38:17.700 --> 38:18.970
It stopped. It stopped.

414
38:20.060 --> 38:21.150
The sky has cleared.

415
38:21.710 --> 38:22.320
The rain has passed.

416
38:22.320 --> 38:22.880
It's finally clear.

417
38:24.510 --> 38:25.480
It's clear.

418
38:33.070 --> 38:33.880
It's so cold.

419
38:38.580 --> 38:39.030
Come on.

420
38:42.440 --> 38:43.290
Let's go.

421
38:44.110 --> 38:45.070
Great.

422
38:47.960 --> 38:48.480
Let's go.

423
38:53.650 --> 38:54.610
A rainbow.

424
38:55.320 --> 38:56.280
There's a rainbow.

425
38:57.220 --> 38:59.010
There's a rainbow over there.

426
39:00.000 --> 39:01.650
It's so beautiful.

427
39:49.140 --> 39:51.460
While the CPC Central Committee was leading the Right Route Army

428
39:51.500 --> 39:53.980
trekking through the grasslands,

429
39:54.540 --> 39:56.980
on August 21, 1935,

430
39:57.240 --> 39:58.680
the 25th Red Army, advancing eastward

431
39:58.700 --> 40:00.740
along the Xi'an-Lanzhou Highway,

432
40:00.920 --> 40:03.440
crossed the Rui River at Sipo Village,

433
40:03.470 --> 40:04.990
west of Jingchuan County seat.

434
40:05.070 --> 40:07.360
They were suddenly ambushed by the 208th Regiment

435
40:07.360 --> 40:09.920
of the 104th Brigade, 35th Division of the Kuomintang Army.

436
40:10.150 --> 40:11.190
After a fierce battle,

437
40:11.550 --> 40:14.230
the 25th Red Army annihilated the regiment

438
40:14.230 --> 40:16.480
and killed Ma Kaiji, the enemy regimental commander.

439
40:16.630 --> 40:17.630
Unfortunately,

440
40:17.970 --> 40:19.970
Comrade Wu Huanxian, the Political Commissar of the army,

441
40:20.070 --> 40:22.080
died heroically in the battle

442
40:22.290 --> 40:24.040
at the age of 28.

443
40:24.610 --> 40:28.160
At this time, the 25th Red Army still hadn't received

444
40:28.190 --> 40:30.280
any news from the 1st and the 4th Front Armies.

445
40:30.870 --> 40:34.140
So they decided to march north to Shaanxi and Gansu as planned,

446
40:34.290 --> 40:36.490
to join forces with the Shaanxi and Gansu Red Army first.

447
40:36.830 --> 40:38.060
Meanwhile,

448
40:38.400 --> 40:40.400
because the Shanghai Central Bureau of the CPC

449
40:40.440 --> 40:42.710
had been severely damaged multiple times,

450
40:42.870 --> 40:45.830
the plan for Chen Yun, who had arrived in Shanghai in July,

451
40:46.230 --> 40:47.800
to use the Shanghai Central Bureau of the CPC

452
40:47.820 --> 40:50.050
to contact Moscow

453
40:50.080 --> 40:51.450
was no longer feasible.

454
40:51.620 --> 40:53.890
The CPC delegation to the Comintern

455
40:53.920 --> 40:56.400
decided to arrange for Chen Yun to go to Moscow

456
40:56.420 --> 40:58.680
to report directly to the Comintern

457
40:58.710 --> 41:00.450
about the Zunyi Conference.

458
41:15.070 --> 41:15.840
Madam,

459
41:15.920 --> 41:17.040
your guest has arrived.

460
41:22.420 --> 41:24.790
[Chen Yun, Member of the Standing Committee of the CPC Politburo,

461
41:24.790 --> 41:27.160
[and Director of the Central White Areas Work Department]

462
41:26.360 --> 41:27.230
Madam Ching-ling.

463
41:27.290 --> 41:29.520
[Soong Ching-ling]

464
41:27.760 --> 41:28.710
You've had a long journey.

465
41:29.150 --> 41:29.960
Please have a seat.

466
41:36.550 --> 41:38.880
Was the journey here smooth?

467
41:39.280 --> 41:40.110
It was fine.

468
41:40.510 --> 41:42.030
There were people tailing me.

469
41:42.230 --> 41:43.230
But I shook them off.

470
41:43.760 --> 41:44.440
Good.

471
41:44.960 --> 41:47.440
What you just said, Madam Ching-ling,

472
41:48.470 --> 41:49.590
sounds

473
41:49.680 --> 41:51.240
very familiar to me.

474
41:51.790 --> 41:52.920
Right.

475
41:53.510 --> 41:55.960
On December 23, 1932,

476
41:56.230 --> 41:57.590
I went to Mr. Lu Xun's house

477
41:57.710 --> 42:00.190
to pick up Comrade Qu Qiubai for transfer.

478
42:00.630 --> 42:03.280
The first thing he said to me was also,

479
42:03.670 --> 42:05.840
"Was the journey here smooth?"

480
42:07.840 --> 42:08.840
In Shanghai,

481
42:09.510 --> 42:11.000
when we meet with you,

482
42:11.590 --> 42:13.530
we inevitably ask this.

483
42:15.800 --> 42:17.280
You've met Mr. Lu Xun.

484
42:18.030 --> 42:20.630
So you know he's a man with a lot on his mind.

485
42:21.030 --> 42:22.150
Not long ago,

486
42:23.710 --> 42:26.090
when he saw the news of Qu Qiubai's sacrifice,

487
42:26.960 --> 42:28.730
he was very sad.

488
42:31.800 --> 42:34.510
Lu Xun and I are deeply concerned

489
42:34.510 --> 42:36.760
about the fate of your Red Army forces on the Westward Expedition.

490
42:37.110 --> 42:38.000
In your ranks,

491
42:38.030 --> 42:40.110
there are many people we know.

492
42:40.800 --> 42:42.030
Our Red Army troops

493
42:42.330 --> 42:43.960
are advancing towards the north.

494
42:54.280 --> 42:55.070
This is

495
42:55.360 --> 42:57.760
a private clinic on Jiujiang Road.

496
42:58.140 --> 43:00.140
The owner's name is Shafick George Hatem.

497
43:00.510 --> 43:01.760
I have arranged

498
43:02.230 --> 43:04.510
for him to escort you.
